course: dictionary
lesson: 16036
title: Words that check: verifier
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A verifier is someone or something that checks whether a thing is true, correct or real. The word comes from verify, which means to check that something is true. If you can say «verify» in a sentence, you can understand «verifier».
explain: The ending -er often means a person or thing that does a job. A teacher teaches, so a verifier verifies. «The fact verifier found one wrong date in the news story.» Here the verifier is a person who checks facts.
explain: In computing, a verifier is a program or tool that checks automatically. «The computer's verifier checked my password and said it was correct.» Nobody had to check by hand; the tool did it for them.
explain: When you meet a new word, look at the context first. Ask what the word is doing in the sentence. Then try your meaning in place of the hard word. If «checks» still makes sense, you have found its meaning.
fact: A verifier is a person or tool that checks that something is true, correct or real.
fact: Verifier comes from the word verify, which means to check that something is true.
fact: A fact verifier checks facts in news stories and other writing.
fact: An age verifier checks how old someone is before they can use a website.
fact: In maths and computing, a verifier can check a proof or an answer automatically.
exercise: «The fact verifier found that the news story had one wrong date.» What is the fact verifier doing? | Taking photos for the newspaper | *Checking that the facts are true and correct | Writing the news story | Selling the newspaper
exercise: What does verify mean? | Print something on paper | Hide something from others | *Check that something is true | Make something up
exercise: Which of these is a verifier? | A kind of bird that sings | A bag for carrying books | *A tool that checks a password automatically | A cake recipe
test: «The computer's verifier checked the answer and said it was correct.» What does the verifier do? | Writes a new story | Deletes the answer | *Checks that the answer is right | Plays music
test: Where does the word verifier come from? | The word ferry | The word veer, meaning to turn | The word very | *The word verify, meaning to check that something is true
exam: «An age verifier stops children from using a website that is not for them.» What does an age verifier check? | What they had for lunch | *How old someone is | What colour their hair is | How tall someone is
